## Why This Is Asked
Tests distributed systems design, failure handling, and financial systems requirements - critical for trading platforms where consistency and recovery are paramount.

## Expected Answer
Candidate should discuss: Saga coordination patterns, compensation strategies, event sourcing for state recovery, handling partial failures, ensuring eventual consistency, and monitoring/observability.

## Code Example
```typescript
// Saga orchestrator with compensation
class OrderSaga {
  async execute(order: Order) {
    try {
      await this.reserveInventory(order);
      await this.processPayment(order);
      await this.executeTrade(order);
    } catch (error) {
      await this.compensate(order);
      throw error;
    }
  }

  private async compensate(order: Order) {
    await Promise.allSettled([
      this.cancelTrade(order),
      this.refundPayment(order),
      this.releaseInventory(order)
    ]);
  }
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Broadcom needs engineers who can design reliable financial systems. This tests understanding of distributed systems, consistency guarantees, and production-scale message queue architecture.

## Expected Answer
Strong candidates discuss: Kafka's exactly-once semantics, idempotent producers, transactional writes, log compaction for deduplication, consumer group coordination, cross-datacenter replication (MirrorMaker), and handling network partitions. They should mention trade-offs between latency and consistency.

## Code Example
```typescript
// Kafka transactional producer setup
const producer = kafka.producer({
  transactionalId: 'financial-tx-producer',
  maxInFlightRequests: 1,
  idempotent: true
});

await producer.initTransactions();

// Exactly-once transaction
await producer.sendTransaction([
  { topic: 'transactions', messages: [{ value: transaction }] }
]);
```
